.TH SDL_HINT_OPENGL_FORCE_SRGB_FRAMEBUFFER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_OPENGL_FORCE_SRGB_FRAMEBUFFER \- A variable controlling whether to force an sRGB-capable OpenGL context.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_OPENGL_FORCE_SRGB_FRAMEBUFFER \(dqSDL_OPENGL_FORCE_SRGB_FRAMEBUFFER\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
At OpenGL context creation time, some platforms can request an sRGB-capable context\[char46] However, sometimes any form of the request can cause surprising results on some drivers, platforms, and hardware\[char46] Usually the surprise is in the form of rendering that is either a little darker or a little brighter than intended\[char46]
.PP
This hint allows the user to override the app\(aqs sRGB requests and either force a specific value, or avoid requesting anything at all, depending on what makes things work correctly for their system\[char46]
.PP
This is meant as a fail-safe; apps should probably not explicitly set this, and most users should not, either\[char46]
.PP
Note that some platforms cannot make this request at all, and on all platforms this request can be denied by the operating system\[char46]
.PP
In addition to attempting to obtain the type of sRGB-capable OpenGL context requested by this hint, SDL will try to force the state of GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB on the new context, if appropriate\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Force a request for an OpenGL context that is _not_ sRGB-capable\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Force a request for an OpenGL context that _is_ sRGB-capable\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqskip\(dq: Don\(aqt make any request for an sRGB-capable context (don\(aqt specify the attribute at all during context creation time)\[char46]
.PP
\(bu any other string is undefined behavior\[char46]
.PP
If unset, or set to an empty string, SDL will make a request using the value the app specified with the
.BR SDL_GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB_CAPABLE
attribute\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an OpenGL context is created\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]2\[char46]

